-- title:
--   Schur's lemma for the GL₃ principal series at equal characters
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a height one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, write $\mathbb{Q}_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, and let $\chi : \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \to \operatorname{Hom}(\mathbb{Q}_v^\times, \mathbb{C}^\times)$ be a triple of monoid homomorphisms (no continuity is imposed) subject to the hypothesis $\chi_0 = \chi_1$ and $\chi_1 = \chi_2$. The space `principalSeries3 v χ` is the complex subspace of functions $f : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ that are locally constant, satisfy $f(u g) = f(g)$ for every upper triangular unipotent $u = \bigl(\begin{smallmatrix} 1&x&z\\ 0&1&y\\ 0&0&1\end{smallmatrix}\bigr)$ with $x,y,z \in \mathbb{Q}_v$, and satisfy $f(\mathrm{diag}(a_0,a_1,a_2)\,g) = \bigl(\prod_i \chi_i(a_i)\bigr)\,\bigl(\lVert a_0\rVert/\lVert a_2\rVert\bigr)\, f(g)$ for all $a_i \in \mathbb{Q}_v^\times$. Let $T$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism of this space which commutes with right translation, in the sense that for every $g \in \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and every $f$ in the space, the function $T(h \mapsto f(hg))$ equals $h \mapsto (Tf)(hg)$. The conclusion is that there is a complex number $c$ with $T = c \cdot \mathrm{id}$.
--
--   This is Schur's lemma for the normalised principal series of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over a $p$-adic field induced from a triple of equal characters of the diagonal torus: the commutant of the right translation action on this induced representation consists of scalars. It is used in the analysis of the cyclic subspace generated by a matrix coefficient, via a bound of at most one on families of linearly independent functionals transforming under the Borel subgroup by the character and half modulus.
